            "stmt_text": "\tmapping = (dma_addr_t *)skb->cb;",
            "location": "context",
            "explanation": "This statement stores DMA mapping address directly in the skb control block (skb->cb). This is a known vulnerability pattern where the DMA mapping pointer may outlive the skb lifetime, leading to use-after-free when the skb is freed but the mapping reference remains accessible. Combined with improper error handling during buffer allocation, this creates a memory corruption attack surface."
          },
